// CDL3INSIDE recognizes the Three Inside Up/Down pattern over bars startIdx
// through endIdx.
//
// A three-candle reversal pattern: a long real body, then a short real body
// totally engulfed by it (a harami), then a third candle of opposite color to
// the first that closes past the first candle's open. Signals a bullish
// reversal (three inside up, significant in a downtrend) or a bearish reversal
// (three inside down, significant in an uptrend).
//
// Formula and more info at https://ta-lib.org/functions/cdl3inside.
//
// Inputs, each at least endIdx+1 long:
//   - inOpen: Open price of each bar.
//   - inHigh: High price of each bar.
//   - inLow: Low price of each bar.
//   - inClose: Close price of each bar.
//
// Outputs, each at least as long as the values written (the input length always
// suffices):
//   - outInteger: +100 for three inside up (bullish reversal, first candle
//     black), -100 for three inside down (bearish reversal, first candle
//     white), 0 when no pattern. Computed as -candlecolor(1st)*100.
//
// Element k of each output is the value at bar BegIdx+k of the returned
// [OutRange], and BegIdx is at least [Core.CDL3INSIDELookback]: a range that
// ends before it returns NBElement 0.
